      "writtenOn": "2026-08-17T15:39:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is safe. The direct callers are close, terminate and the keepalive timer. close and terminate ignore the result and close the session right after.\n\nThe keepalive is harmless. A dropped one is ignored and the timer keeps rescheduling, so keepalives resume once the channel drains. And a keepalive is only needed when nothing else is going to the peer, which is not the case during a bulk advertisement.\n\nI also added a javadoc to the method stating that it drops when the channel is full and is only for droppable control messages, and that anything needing delivery must go through the limiter.",
      "parentUuid": "1f620f18_cd487d62",
      "revId": "66724b23c36781a148ed887ca713031204c10013",
